---
/**
 * medicare-advantage-total-cost-estimator.astro
 * Tool 2: Medicare Advantage Total-Cost Estimator
 *
 * URL: /tools/medicare-advantage-total-cost-estimator/
 * Title: Medicare Advantage Cost Estimator 2026 | Seniors Audit    [54 chars]
 * Meta:  Free 2026 Medicare Advantage cost estimator. See typical-year
 *        range and worst-case cap. No signup needed.                 [107 chars]
 *
 * 2026 Verified Figures — confirmed against CMS August 15 2026:
 *   Part B standard monthly premium   : $202.90  [CMS 2026 Parts A & B Premiums Fact Sheet]
 *   Part B annual                      : $2,434.80
 *   MA in-network MOOP ceiling (2026)  : $9,250   [CMS 2026 MA & Part D Rate Announcement]
 *   Part D OOP cap (2026, IRA)         : $2,100   [Same announcement]
 *
 * All verified source links used below are live as of August 15 2026.
 *
 * Compliance (Prompt 2 Section 0):
 *   [x] No carrier or plan names
 *   [x] No contact-info collection
 *   [x] All calcs client-side only
 *   [x] No fake urgency or dark patterns
 *   [x] SHIP pathway for personalized help
 *   [x] All citation URLs verified live August 15 2026
 *   [x] Internal links open in new tab
 *   [x] DOB input with dynamic age calculation
 */

import ToolLayout from '@layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import NoSignupStatement from '@components/common/NoSignupStatement.astro';

const lastReviewed = 'August 2026';
const slug         = 'medicare-advantage-total-cost-estimator';
const canonical    = `https://www.seniorsaudit.com/tools/${slug}/`;

const US_STATES = [
  'Alabama','Alaska','Arizona','Arkansas','California','Colorado','Connecticut',
  'Delaware','Florida','Georgia','Hawaii','Idaho','Illinois','Indiana','Iowa',
  'Kansas','Kentucky','Louisiana','Maine','Maryland','Massachusetts','Michigan',
  'Minnesota','Mississippi','Missouri','Montana','Nebraska','Nevada',
  'New Hampshire','New Jersey','New Mexico','New York','North Carolina',
  'North Dakota','Ohio','Oklahoma','Oregon','Pennsylvania','Rhode Island',
  'South Carolina','South Dakota','Tennessee','Texas','Utah','Vermont',
  'Virginia','Washington','West Virginia','Wisconsin','Wyoming',
  'District of Columbia',
];

const faqs = [
  { question: 'What is the Medicare Advantage out-of-pocket maximum for 2026?',
    answer: 'CMS set the in-network MA MOOP ceiling at $9,250 for 2026. Individual plans may set a lower cap. Once you reach your plan\'s MOOP, covered in-network services cost $0 for the rest of the year. Prescription drug costs have a separate $2,100 Part D cap. Source: CMS 2026 MA and Part D Rate Announcement.' },
  { question: 'Do $0 premium Medicare Advantage plans mean Medicare is free?',
    answer: 'No. Even with a $0 MA plan premium, you still owe the Medicare Part B premium — $202.90 per month ($2,434.80 per year) in 2026. This is deducted from your Social Security benefit or billed directly. The $0 refers only to the MA plan\'s own premium charged on top of Part B.' },
  { question: 'Does the Medicare Advantage MOOP cover prescription drug costs?',
    answer: 'No. The $9,250 MOOP covers Part A and Part B medical cost-sharing only. Prescription drug costs under Part D have a completely separate $2,100 out-of-pocket cap in 2026 under the Inflation Reduction Act. In a true worst-case year you could owe both caps plus the Part B premium.' },
  { question: 'What happens if I need out-of-network care with Medicare Advantage?',
    answer: 'HMO plans generally provide no coverage for non-emergency out-of-network care. PPO plans cover out-of-network care at higher cost-sharing, and may have a higher or separate out-of-network MOOP. Always review your plan\'s Evidence of Coverage before seeing an out-of-network provider.' },
  { question: 'Do I still pay the Part B premium with Medicare Advantage?',
    answer: 'Yes, always. Every Medicare beneficiary on MA still owes the Part B premium — $202.90/month in 2026. Some plans offer a Part B premium giveback, but that is plan-specific and not guaranteed. If you owe IRMAA, your Part B cost is higher regardless of your MA plan.' },
  { question: 'What is the difference between HMO and PPO Medicare Advantage plans?',
    answer: 'HMO plans require in-network providers and referrals for specialists, with lower premiums and more predictable costs. PPO plans allow out-of-network care without referrals, at higher cost-sharing. HMOs typically have lower MOOPs. Find plans at medicare.gov/plan-compare.' },
  { question: 'Can I switch from Medicare Advantage back to Original Medicare?',
    answer: 'Yes. You can switch during Annual Enrollment (Oct 15 to Dec 7) or MA Open Enrollment (Jan 1 to Mar 31). However, switching back to Original Medicare makes getting Medigap coverage harder — most states allow medical underwriting outside your initial enrollment window.' },
  { question: 'How does IRMAA affect Medicare Advantage costs?',
    answer: 'IRMAA surcharges apply to your Part B and Part D premiums — not to your MA plan premium. If your 2024 MAGI exceeded $109,000 (single) or $218,000 (joint), you owe $81.20 to $487.00 extra per month on Part B, on top of any MA plan costs.' },
  { question: 'Do Medicare Advantage costs change every year?',
    answer: 'Yes. MA plans can change premiums, copays, MOOP amounts, drug formularies, and networks annually. Review your Annual Notice of Change letter every September and compare plans at medicare.gov/plan-compare during the Oct 15 to Dec 7 enrollment window each year.' },
];

const howToSteps = [
  { name: 'Enter your date of birth and state',
    text: 'Your age provides context for the estimate. Your state flags counties with limited MA plan availability or high-cost markets. Actual plan options depend on your specific ZIP code.' },
  { name: 'Select your expected healthcare usage level',
    text: 'Low = routine checkups only. Moderate = 1-2 specialist visits or minor procedures. High = surgery, hospitalization, or chronic specialist management expected this year.' },
  { name: 'Choose your out-of-network care frequency',
    text: 'This affects whether the $9,250 MOOP is your real worst case. HMO plans do not cover non-emergency out-of-network care. If you answered Often, read the OON warning in your results carefully.' },
  { name: 'Select your drug usage tier',
    text: 'Drug costs are tracked separately from medical costs under MA. They have their own $2,100 cap under the Inflation Reduction Act. This proxy gives you an estimated drug cost range.' },
  { name: 'Review your two numbers',
    text: 'Typical Year is a DECISION SUPPORT estimate using illustrative copay proxies. Worst Case is built from verified CMS facts — MOOP + Part B premium + Part D cap.' },
];
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Medicare Advantage Cost Estimator 2026 | Seniors Audit"
  description="Free 2026 Medicare Advantage cost estimator. See your typical-year range and worst-case cap. No signup needed."
  canonical={canonical}
  faqs={faqs}
  howToSteps={howToSteps}
>

<!-- BREADCRUMB -->
<nav class="mat-bc" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/" class="mat-bc-link">Home</a>
  <span aria-hidden="true"> &rsaquo; </span>
  <a href="/tools/" class="mat-bc-link">Tools</a>
  <span aria-hidden="true"> &rsaquo; </span>
  <span>Medicare Advantage Cost Estimator</span>
</nav>

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="mat-hero">
  <p class="mat-reviewed">Last reviewed by the Seniors Audit research team on <time datetime="2026-08">{lastReviewed}</time></p>
  <h1 class="mat-h1">Medicare Advantage Total-Cost Estimator 2026</h1>
  <p class="mat-subtitle">See your realistic typical-year range <em>and</em> your worst-case in-network cap before you enroll.</p>

  <div class="mat-qa" role="note" aria-label="Quick Answer">
    <p class="mat-qa-label">Quick Answer</p>
    <p class="mat-qa-text">In 2026 the CMS-set Medicare Advantage in-network out-of-pocket ceiling is <strong>$9,250</strong> — that is your worst-case medical cost, not counting the Part B premium ($202.90/mo) every beneficiary still owes. Most people in healthy years pay far less. Prescription drug costs have a <strong>separate $2,100 cap</strong> under the Inflation Reduction Act.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="mat-problem">Medicare Advantage plans advertise $0 premiums prominently, which creates a common misunderstanding: that Medicare Advantage is free. It is not. You still owe the Part B premium every month, you pay copays on nearly every service, and if you have a serious health event you could owe up to $9,250 before your plan covers 100%. This tool shows you both numbers — the realistic middle and the hard worst case — so you can budget accurately.</p>

  <div class="mat-covers">
    <p class="mat-covers-label">What this tool covers:</p>
    <ul class="mat-covers-list">
      <li>Your typical-year estimated cost range based on expected healthcare and drug usage</li>
      <li>Your verified worst-case in-network cap ($9,250 MOOP — a direct CMS number)</li>
      <li>Why $0 premium plans still cost $2,434.80/year minimum in Part B premiums</li>
      <li>Out-of-network cost warnings for HMO vs PPO plan types</li>
      <li>How prescription drug costs interact with (but are separate from) the MOOP</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<NoSignupStatement />

<!-- TOOL -->
<div id="mat-tool" class="mat-tool">

  <div class="mat-tool-hdr">
    <h2 class="mat-tool-h2">Estimate Your Medicare Advantage Annual Costs</h2>
    <p class="mat-tool-intro">All calculations run in your browser. Nothing you enter is stored or transmitted. The $9,250 MOOP and $202.90 Part B premium are official CMS figures. Copay proxies are illustrative estimates, clearly labeled throughout.</p>
    <div class="mat-badge-legend">
      <span class="mat-badge mat-fact">FACT</span> = Official government figure, cited.&nbsp;
      <span class="mat-badge mat-est">ESTIMATE</span> = Illustrative proxy, varies by plan.&nbsp;
      <span class="mat-badge mat-ds">DECISION SUPPORT</span> = Educational range.
    </div>
    <div class="mat-carrier-warn">
      <strong>Important:</strong> This estimates a typical plan structure — not any specific plan. MA costs vary significantly by carrier and county. Always verify at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a> using your ZIP code.
    </div>
  </div>

  <form id="mat-form" novalidate>

    <!-- DOB -->
    <div class="mat-field">
      <span class="mat-label">Your Date of Birth <small class="mat-hint">(used to calculate your age)</small></span>
      <div class="mat-dob-row">
        <div class="mat-dob-col">
          <label for="mat-m" class="mat-dob-label">Month</label>
          <select id="mat-m" class="mat-sel" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-dob-err">
            <option value="">— MM —</option>
            <option value="1">January</option><option value="2">February</option><option value="3">March</option>
            <option value="4">April</option><option value="5">May</option><option value="6">June</option>
            <option value="7">July</option><option value="8">August</option><option value="9">September</option>
            <option value="10">October</option><option value="11">November</option><option value="12">December</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="mat-dob-col">
          <label for="mat-d" class="mat-dob-label">Day</label>
          <select id="mat-d" class="mat-sel" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-dob-err">
            <option value="">— DD —</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="mat-dob-col mat-dob-yr">
          <label for="mat-y" class="mat-dob-label">Year</label>
          <input type="number" id="mat-y" min="1939" max="1966" placeholder="YYYY" class="mat-inp" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-dob-err" autocomplete="bday-year" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="mat-age-disp" class="mat-age-disp" style="display:none;" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <span id="mat-dob-err" class="mat-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>

    <!-- State -->
    <div class="mat-field">
      <label for="mat-state" class="mat-label">Your State</label>
      <select id="mat-state" class="mat-sel" aria-required="true">
        <option value="">— Select your state —</option>
        {US_STATES.map(s => <option value={s}>{s}</option>)}
      </select>
      <p class="mat-hint-txt">MA plan availability and costs vary by county. See real plans in your ZIP at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Healthcare usage -->
    <fieldset class="mat-fs">
      <legend class="mat-legend">Expected Healthcare Usage This Year</legend>
      <p class="mat-fs-hint">Not sure? Read our <a href="/medicare/what-is-medicare-part-c/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">guide to how Medicare Advantage works</a> or compare options with the <a href="/tools/medicare-advantage-vs-original-medicare-cost-checker/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">MA vs Original Medicare cost checker</a>.</p>
      <div class="mat-rg" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-usage-err">
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-usage" value="low" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Low</strong><span class="mat-rsub">Routine checkups and preventive care only &mdash; no specialist visits, procedures, or hospitalizations</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-usage" value="moderate" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Moderate</strong><span class="mat-rsub">1&ndash;2 specialist visits or minor procedures expected &mdash; no hospitalization</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-usage" value="high" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>High</strong><span class="mat-rsub">Surgery, hospitalization, or ongoing specialist management for a chronic condition expected this year</span></span></label>
      </div>
      <span id="mat-usage-err" class="mat-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </fieldset>

    <!-- Out-of-network -->
    <fieldset class="mat-fs">
      <legend class="mat-legend">Do You Expect to Need Out-of-Network Care?</legend>
      <p class="mat-fs-hint">Traveling frequently, a key specialist not in any local MA network, or splitting time between two states? Read <a href="/medicare/medicare-vs-medicare-advantage/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">how MA networks work vs Original Medicare</a>.</p>
      <div class="mat-rg" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-oon-err">
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-oon" value="rarely" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Rarely</strong><span class="mat-rsub">All my doctors and specialists are in-network</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-oon" value="sometimes" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Sometimes</strong><span class="mat-rsub">I may occasionally see an out-of-network provider or travel for care</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-oon" value="often" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Often</strong><span class="mat-rsub">I frequently travel, split time between states, or have a key specialist not in any local MA network</span></span></label>
      </div>
      <span id="mat-oon-err" class="mat-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </fieldset>

    <!-- Drug usage -->
    <fieldset class="mat-fs">
      <legend class="mat-legend">Expected Prescription Drug Usage</legend>
      <p class="mat-fs-hint">Drug costs under MA are tracked separately and have their own $2,100 cap. Read our <a href="/medicare/what-is-medicare-part-d/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">guide to how Medicare Part D works</a>. For exact costs, use <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a> with your medication list.</p>
      <div class="mat-rg" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="mat-drug-err">
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-drug" value="none" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>None</strong><span class="mat-rsub">No regular prescriptions &mdash; drug proxy: $0/yr</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-drug" value="low" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Low</strong><span class="mat-rsub">1&ndash;2 generic drugs &mdash; drug proxy: $200&ndash;$500/yr</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-drug" value="moderate" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>Moderate</strong><span class="mat-rsub">3&ndash;5 mixed generic and brand-name drugs &mdash; drug proxy: $800&ndash;$1,500/yr</span></span></label>
        <label class="mat-rl"><input type="radio" name="mat-drug" value="high" class="mat-r" /><span class="mat-rc"><strong>High</strong><span class="mat-rsub">Specialty drugs or 6+ medications &mdash; capped at 2026 Part D OOP limit: $2,100/yr</span></span></label>
      </div>
      <span id="mat-drug-err" class="mat-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="mat-btn-row">
      <button type="button" id="mat-calc" class="mat-btn-p" aria-controls="mat-results">Calculate My Medicare Advantage Costs</button>
      <button type="button" id="mat-reset" class="mat-btn-s">Start Over</button>
    </div>

  </form>

  <!-- RESULTS -->
  <div id="mat-results" class="mat-results" style="display:none;" role="region" aria-label="Your Medicare Advantage cost estimate" aria-live="polite">

    <div id="mat-oon-warn" class="mat-oon-warn" style="display:none;" role="alert">
      <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Out-of-Network Warning</strong>
      <p>You indicated you frequently need out-of-network care. The $9,250 worst-case MOOP below applies only to <em>in-network</em> services. For HMO plans, out-of-network care (other than emergencies) is generally not covered at all. For PPO plans, out-of-network costs often have a higher or separate MOOP. This tool cannot capture your true worst case. Review the plan's Evidence of Coverage at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a> before enrolling.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="mat-state-note" class="mat-state-note" style="display:none;" role="note"></div>

    <!-- Two-card display -->
    <div class="mat-two-col">

      <div class="mat-card mat-card-typ">
        <p class="mat-card-lbl">Typical Year</p>
        <p class="mat-card-bdg"><span class="mat-badge mat-ds">DECISION SUPPORT</span></p>
        <p class="mat-card-range">
          <span id="mat-typ-lo" class="mat-num">&#8212;</span>
          <span class="mat-dash"> &ndash; </span>
          <span id="mat-typ-hi" class="mat-num">&#8212;</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mat-card-sub">Estimated annual range at your usage level</p>
        <p class="mat-card-mo">&#8776; <span id="mat-typ-mo-lo">&#8212;</span> &ndash; <span id="mat-typ-mo-hi">&#8212;</span> per month</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mat-card mat-card-wst">
        <p class="mat-card-lbl">Worst Case (In-Network)</p>
        <p class="mat-card-bdg"><span class="mat-badge mat-fact">FACT</span></p>
        <p class="mat-card-range"><span id="mat-wst" class="mat-num mat-num-wst">&#8212;</span></p>
        <p class="mat-card-sub">$9,250 MOOP + $2,434.80 Part B + $2,100 drug cap</p>
        <p class="mat-card-mo">&#8776; <span id="mat-wst-mo">&#8212;</span> per month</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Breakdown -->
    <div class="mat-bk">
      <h3 class="mat-bk-h3">What Makes Up Your Estimate</h3>
      <div class="mat-tbl-wrap">
        <table class="mat-tbl" aria-label="Cost breakdown">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Cost Component</th><th>Typical Year</th><th>Worst Case</th><th>Type</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Medicare Part B Premium</td>
              <td>$2,434.80</td><td>$2,434.80</td>
              <td><span class="mat-badge mat-fact">FACT</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="mat-alt">
              <td>MA Plan Premium (baseline)</td>
              <td>$0 (many plans charge more)</td><td>$0</td>
              <td><span class="mat-badge mat-est">ESTIMATE</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td id="mat-bk-cop-lbl">Medical Copays / Coinsurance</td>
              <td id="mat-bk-cop">&#8212;</td><td>Up to $9,250 MOOP</td>
              <td><span class="mat-badge mat-ds">DECISION SUPPORT</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="mat-alt">
              <td>Prescription Drugs (Part D)</td>
              <td id="mat-bk-drug">&#8212;</td><td>Up to $2,100 (separate cap)</td>
              <td><span class="mat-badge mat-est">ESTIMATE</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="mat-total-row">
              <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
              <td><strong id="mat-bk-tot-typ">&#8212;</strong></td>
              <td><strong id="mat-bk-tot-wst">&#8212;</strong></td>
              <td></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mat-bk-note">True worst case = $2,434.80 (Part B) + $9,250 (MOOP) + $2,100 (Part D cap) = <strong>$13,784.80</strong>. Drug costs are shown separately because they are capped by a different program than the MOOP.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Part B box -->
    <div class="mat-partb-box" role="note">
      <strong>Why you still owe $202.90/month even with a $0 premium plan</strong>
      <p>Medicare Advantage plans contract with CMS to deliver your Part A and Part B benefits. You must remain enrolled in Part B to have any MA plan, which means the Part B premium is always owed to Medicare directly. Some MA plans offer a "Part B premium giveback" that offsets part of this — but that is plan-specific and not included in this baseline estimate. If you owe IRMAA, your Part B cost is even higher. Use our <a href="/tools/medicare-irmaa-calculator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">IRMAA calculator</a> to find your exact 2026 surcharge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mat-reset-row">
      <button type="button" id="mat-reset2" class="mat-btn-s mat-btn-sm">&#8592; Start Over</button>
      <a href="/tools/original-medicare-medigap-part-d-cost-estimator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-compare-link">Compare with Original Medicare + Medigap &#8594;</a>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /results -->

</div><!-- /tool -->

<!-- ACTION PLAN -->
<section class="mat-sec" aria-labelledby="mat-act-h2">
  <h2 id="mat-act-h2" class="mat-sec-h2">Your Medicare Advantage Action Plan</h2>
  <p class="mat-sec-intro">Once you have reviewed your estimate, here are the specific steps to take before choosing a Medicare Advantage plan.</p>
  <ol class="mat-act-list">
    <li><strong>Verify every doctor and hospital in the plan's network.</strong> At <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a>, look up each of your current providers by name in the plan's directory before enrolling — not after.</li>
    <li><strong>Check your drug formulary before enrolling.</strong> Enter your exact medications at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a> to see real drug costs for each plan. Do not assume your current drugs are covered.</li>
    <li><strong>Calculate your IRMAA first.</strong> If your 2024 MAGI exceeded $109,000 (single) or $218,000 (joint), your Part B cost is higher than the standard $202.90. Use our <a href="/tools/medicare-irmaa-calculator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">IRMAA calculator</a> before finalizing your healthcare budget. Not sure of your MAGI? Use the <a href="/tools/magi-for-medicare-calculator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">MAGI for Medicare calculator</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the Evidence of Coverage for any plan you are seriously considering.</strong> Look specifically for the out-of-network MOOP — it may be much higher than the in-network MOOP, or unlimited for HMO plans.</li>
    <li><strong>Compare this estimate against Original Medicare + Medigap.</strong> Use our <a href="/tools/original-medicare-medigap-part-d-cost-estimator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">Original Medicare + Medigap + Part D Cost Estimator</a> to see how the two paths compare for your specific situation. The right answer depends on your health, budget, and provider preferences.</li>
    <li><strong>Talk to a free SHIP counselor before enrolling.</strong> State Health Insurance Assistance Programs provide free, unbiased counseling on all plan options in your county. Find yours at <a href="https://www.shiphelp.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mat-link">shiphelp.org</a> or call <strong>1-877-839-2675</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<!-- HOW TO USE -->
<section class="mat-sec" aria-labelledby="mat-howto-h2">
  <h2 id="mat-howto-h2" class="mat-sec-h2">How to Use This Tool</h2>
  <ol class="mat-howto">
    {howToSteps.map((step, i) => (
      <li class="mat-howto-item">
        <span class="mat-step-num" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span>
        <div><strong class="mat-step-title">{step.name}</strong><p class="mat-step-text">{step.text}</p></div>
